  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You conjure a group of intangible, orderly spirits that look like a Medium group of modrons or other Constructs, in an unoccupied space you can see within range. They last for the duration.</p><p>When you cast the spell, and as a Magic action on your later turns, you can have the spirits target one creature or object you can see within 5 feet of them with one of the following effects.</p><p><strong>Clockwork Force.</strong> The target makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 Force damage on a failure or half as much on a success.</p><p><strong>Orderly Ward.</strong> The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to 1d6 plus your spellcasting ability modifier.</p><p>When you move on your turn, you can also move the spirits up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Both the damage and the Temporary Hit Points increase by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 3.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
